### Controller minus baseline

Each row is the difference of the group's metric from the baseline's
(group minus baseline; negative means lower than baseline), with a
two-sided t-distribution interval at the {{ ci_level_pct }} percent level.
Seed-paired contrasts use the per-seed differences of common-random-number
replicates (docs/CONTROLLER_COMPARISON.md); when the seed sets differ the
interval is Welch's unequal-variance interval on the difference of means.
A contrast is resolved when its interval excludes zero; an unresolved
contrast is not evidence of an effect in either direction.
